From af40a20a3913b244503ffd74209f2377d6eef757 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CIQ Kernel Automation <ciq_kernel_automation@ciq.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:30:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: af_alg - Cap AEAD AD length to 0x80000000

jira VULN-189980
cve CVE-2026-52972
commit-author Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
commit e4c06479d7059888adf2f22bc1ebcf053bf691a2

In order to prevent arithmetic overflows when checking the TX
buffer size, cap the associated data length to 0x80000000.

	Reported-by: Yiming Qian <yimingqian591@gmail.com>
Fixes: 400c40cf78da ("crypto: algif - add AEAD support")
	Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
(cherry picked from commit e4c06479d7059888adf2f22bc1ebcf053bf691a2)
Signed-off-by: CIQ Kernel Automation <ciq_kernel_automation@ciq.com>
---
 crypto/af_alg.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crypto/af_alg.c b/crypto/af_alg.c
index 96ac49a4d62b4..80468cac0d5bb 100644
--- a/crypto/af_alg.c
+++ b/crypto/af_alg.c
@@ -476,6 +476,8 @@ static int af_alg_cmsg_send(struct msghdr *msg, struct af_alg_control *con)
 			if (cmsg->cmsg_len < CMSG_LEN(sizeof(u32)))
 				return -EINVAL;
 			con->aead_assoclen = *(u32 *)CMSG_DATA(cmsg);
+			if (con->aead_assoclen >= 0x80000000u)
+				return -EINVAL;
 			break;
 
 		default:
-- 
2.52.0

